# MOBILE_SPACING_SYSTEM
## Portfolio Monitoring Frontend
Version: 1.0  
Scope: sm ≤ 640px  
Mode: Ultra Compact Fintech Spacing Model  

---

## 1. Purpose

Define a strict mobile-first spacing system optimized for:

- High financial data density  
- Reduced vertical scroll  
- Predictable layout rhythm  
- Compact exchange-style interface  
- Elimination of decorative whitespace  

This specification applies ONLY to mobile (≤640px).  
Tablet and desktop breakpoints must remain unaffected.

---

## 2. Core Principles

1. Use a 4px grid system.  
2. Minimize vertical whitespace.  
3. Keep sections tightly grouped.  
4. Avoid marketing-style spacing.  
5. Maintain consistent rhythm across components.  

Mobile spacing must prioritize information per pixel.

---

## 3. Base Grid System

Base unit: 4px  

Allowed spacing increments:

4px  
8px  
12px  
16px  

Avoid spacing above 20px on mobile.

---

## 4. Section Vertical Spacing

Between major sections:

12px–16px maximum  

Implementation reference:

- mt-3  
- mb-3  
- mt-4  
- mb-4  

Never use:

- mt-8  
- mb-8  
- space-y-10  
- my-12  

---

## 5. Internal Block Spacing

Label to value: 4px  
Value to change indicator: 4px  
Section title to content: 8px  
Card header to body: 8px  

Keep internal grouping tight.

---

## 6. Card Padding

Mobile cards must use:

p-3  

or

px-3 py-3  

Avoid:

p-6  
p-8  

Cards must feel compact and dense.

---

## 7. Header Spacing

Header height:

56px maximum  

Padding:

px-3 py-2  

Remove excess vertical padding.

---

## 8. Balance Block Spacing

Structure:

Label  
Balance  
Change indicator  

Spacing:

6–8px between elements  
12px bottom margin  

Avoid excessive vertical expansion.

---

## 9. Chart Container Spacing

Chart height:

160px–200px  

Margins:

mt-3  
mb-3  

Internal padding:

px-3 py-2  

Remove unnecessary wrapper div spacing.

---

## 10. Button Spacing

Button height:

h-9  

Spacing between buttons:

gap-2  

Maximum vertical gap between button group and next section:

12px  

Avoid oversized CTA spacing.

---

## 11. Asset Row Spacing

Target row height:

48px–56px  

Row padding:

px-3 py-2  

Spacing between rows:

8px  

No large gaps between asset items.

---

## 12. Viewport Density Requirement

Above-the-fold must include:

✓ Portfolio balance  
✓ Chart  
✓ At least 2–3 assets  

If first viewport shows excessive empty space, spacing is incorrect.

---

## 13. Forbidden Mobile Patterns

Do NOT use:

py-8  
py-10  
my-10  
my-12  
space-y-12  
empty spacer divs  

No artificial whitespace blocks.

---

## 14. Layout Rhythm Pattern

Recommended stacking pattern:

Header  
↓ 8px  
Balance  
↓ 12px  
Chart  
↓ 12px  
Buttons  
↓ 12px  
Asset List  

Maintain consistency throughout.

---

## 15. Implementation Strategy

Mobile-first Tailwind structure:

<div className="px-3 py-2 md:px-6 md:py-4">

Mobile is default.  
Larger breakpoints override upward.

Never shrink desktop spacing into mobile.  
Always build upward from compact mobile.

---

## 16. Performance Considerations

Spacing must:

- Avoid layout shift  
- Avoid cumulative large margins  
- Maintain scroll efficiency  
- Keep first viewport dense  

---

## 17. Final Constraint

Spacing is a structural rule, not aesthetic preference.  
Do not increase vertical whitespace on mobile for visual comfort.

Financial dashboards require density, clarity, and precision.

END